course: dictionary
lesson: 11856
title: Spotting the fake: bogus
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Bogus means fake or not real. Something bogus pretends to be something it is not. The words around it give you clues about what is being faked.
explain: «The email from the bank was bogus, because the bank never sent it.» The clue is never sent: the email pretends to be from the bank, but it is not. Try your meaning in the sentence: the email was fake, and that still makes sense.
explain: Bogus is also slang. «That's so bogus!» means something is unfair or rubbish, not that it is fake. The sentence and the speaker's tone tell you which meaning fits.
fact: Bogus means fake or not real, pretending to be something it is not.
fact: «A bogus caller» pretends to be from the bank or the gas company.
fact: «Bogus websites» look real, but scammers make them to steal money or personal details.
fact: Slang: «That's so bogus!» means unfair or rubbish, especially in American English.
fact: If someone calls claiming to be from your bank, hang up and phone the number you already know to check.
exercise: «The website asked for my password, but it was bogus.» What does bogus mean here? | Lovely and bright | Old and broken | Very fast | *Fake, pretending to be real
exercise: «A bogus caller said he was from the gas company.» Which word tells you the caller was not really from the gas company? | gas | caller | company | *bogus
exercise: Sam says, «That maths test was so bogus, the teacher marked me wrong for no reason.» What does bogus suggest here? | Fake, pretending to be real | Very sparkly | Not finished yet | *Unfair or rubbish
test: Which of these is a bogus caller? | A friend texting about football | *Someone who pretends to be from the bank to get your details | The dentist ringing to move your appointment | Your gran ringing to ask how school went
test: Mia says, «That price was bogus. The shop said it was free, then charged me.» What does bogus mean here? | Brand new | *Unfair | Very cheap, like a bargain | Shiny and bright
exam: Why should you be careful with a bogus website? | It is always run by a bank | It is the official website of your school | It is always free to use | *It may look real but be a scam to steal your money
